{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7KeyCqmtdZkT8c2fWFn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The letter is 327 words. I didn't mention the $9,000 because he already knows what the role pays.\n\n<final_document>\nSubject: Request for promotion to Senior Paralegal\n\nDear David,\n\nI'm writing to ask you to consider me for promotion to senior paralegal in the January review cycle. I have been a paralegal in the litigation group for five years.\n\nIn 2025 I supported four lawyers on 23 cases, two of which went to trial. I billed 1,640 hours, against the group's target of 1,550.\n\nA senior paralegal supervises the group's other paralegals, and I have already done much of the groundwork for that. I trained all three paralegals the group has hired in the last two years, so I know how each of them works and where new hires usually need help. If I'm promoted, I'll hold a short weekly check-in with the paralegals I supervise to go over upcoming deadlines and workload before problems build up. I will also finish the state paralegal certification by June 2027.\n\nIn 2023 I built the group's court-deadline tracking sheet, and two other groups in the firm now use it. You should also know about a mistake I made in it. Last March I entered a filing deadline wrong. Another paralegal caught it, and we filed two hours before the court's cutoff. That was too close. In April I added a second-person check to the sheet, so every deadline is now confirmed by someone other than the person who entered it. Since then, about 600 entries have gone through the sheet with no wrong or missed deadlines. I can't promise I'll never make another error. But the sheet is now set up so that one person's error is caught before it reaches the court. That is the kind of system I would bring to supervising the group's paralegals.\n\nI'd welcome the chance to talk this through with you in person before the January review. Please let me know a time that works for you.\n\nThank you for considering my request.\n\nBest regards,\n\n[Your name]\nParalegal, Litigation Group\n</final_document>\n\nA few things to check before you send it:\n\n- **The paralegal who left:** I left out that one of the three people you trained left after 8 months. David will probably know about it already. If you know why they left and it had nothing to do with their training (a move, a different career), I'd suggest adding one sentence so he doesn't wonder. If you don't know why, I'd leave it out.\n- **The March error:** I put it in the letter even though he may not know about it. If he hears about it from someone else, it will look like you hid it. Coming from you, it's your best evidence that you fix problems at the source.\n- **Your name:** Replace the placeholder in the signature. Also confirm that \"2025\" and \"June 2027\" match how you count \"last year\" and \"next June.\""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":721,"cache_read_input_tokens":10272,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":721},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9cf1a9b-0d90-4f76-bd26-765993972f93","uuid":"aef43888-1aad-404f-9f09-7dc3c2d848cf","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:32:55.054Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7Kexzwkt6qeaCQWVLor"}
